# Architecture decision records

MADR format. One file per decision: `NNNN-short-kebab-title.md`, numbered in order, never renumbered.

Write an ADR when a decision is **structural**: it constrains future work, it was contested, or reversing it would be expensive. Not for routine choices.

```markdown
# NNNN. Title

- Status: accepted | superseded by ADR-NNNN | deprecated
- Date: YYYY-MM-DD

## Context
What forced a decision. The constraints in play.

## Decision
What was decided, in the active voice.

## Consequences
What this makes easy, what it makes hard, what it forecloses.

## Alternatives considered
What else was on the table and why it lost.
```

Parallel branches produce **colliding ADR numbers** and git reports no conflict. Check the highest number on the integration branch, not on yours, before claiming one.
